Flight tracks: Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0

The ADS-B extracts in this folder (data/flights/<city>/raw/*.trace.json.gz) and the flight tracks derived from them
(public/data/<city>/flights/*.json, *.bin) are made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Source: the adsb.lol historical archive (globe_history), https://www.adsb.lol/docs/open-data/historical/ and
https://github.com/adsblol/globe_history_2025 , https://github.com/adsblol/globe_history_2026 , published by adsb.lol
under ODbL 1.0 ("use it freely, just keep it open"). Contains information from adsb.lol, made available under the ODbL.

What was done to it (scripts/fetch_adsb_day.py, scripts/find_arrivals.py, scripts/bake_flight.py): one aircraft's
trace_full file(s) for one UTC day were extracted unchanged; the tracks were filtered to ADS-B positions, gated for
outliers, smoothed to 1 Hz, their heights calibrated on the runway, and attitude, configuration and lights inferred
(each channel's provenance is in the track's header). The release tag and the aircraft's ICAO address of each track
are in data/flights/<city>/selection.json.

Share-alike: if you publicly use an adapted version of these tracks, you must also offer that adapted database under
the ODbL. Keep this notice with the data.

Other data that enter the bake: weather reports from the Iowa Environmental Mesonet ASOS archive
(https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/), public domain, credit appreciated; runway data from the FAA NASR subscription,
a US government work.
